# Boot stage probe.
#
# The device hangs before the boot animation with no adb and an empty pstore, so
# there is no way to see how far init gets. The charging LED is the one output
# channel that needs neither a display, a USB connection nor a mounted /data.
#
# Each init stage sets a distinct blink rate. Whatever the LED is doing when the
# device wedges tells you the last stage that ran:
#
#   very slow  2s/2s  init
#   slow       1s/1s  fs           (partitions mounted)
#   medium   500ms    post-fs
#   fast     200ms    post-fs-data (/data mounted and usable)
#   very fast 100ms   zygote-start
#   off               boot         (init finished - problem is above init)
#
# There is deliberately no early-init entry. /sys/class/leds/charging is created
# by leds-indicator-pwm.ko (dtbo: compatible "qcom,indicator-pwm-led", label
# "charging"), which is entry 68 of 69 in modules.load and is loaded from
# /vendor/lib/modules by vendor.init_modprobe - an *asynchronous* service that
# init.target.rc starts in its own "on early-init". At early-init the sysfs node
# therefore does not exist yet and every write to it is silently dropped.
#
# That is what made the first version of this file useless: it wrote brightness
# exactly once, at early-init, so brightness stayed 0. The timer trigger blinks
# between 0 and the current brightness, so setting delay_on/delay_off later
# produced no visible blink at any stage - a healthy boot looked identical to a
# hung one. Every stage now re-asserts brightness for that reason.
#
# "No LED at all" consequently means either that init never reached "init", or
# that the module never loaded. It is not by itself evidence about first-stage
# init. Prefer /sys/fs/pstore/console-ramoops-0 read from recovery; this is only
# a fallback for when that comes up empty.
#
# Remove this file once the hang is understood.

on init
    write /sys/class/leds/charging/trigger timer
    write /sys/class/leds/charging/brightness 255
    write /sys/class/leds/charging/delay_on 2000
    write /sys/class/leds/charging/delay_off 2000

on fs
    write /sys/class/leds/charging/trigger timer
    write /sys/class/leds/charging/brightness 255
    write /sys/class/leds/charging/delay_on 1000
    write /sys/class/leds/charging/delay_off 1000

on post-fs
    write /sys/class/leds/charging/trigger timer
    write /sys/class/leds/charging/brightness 255
    write /sys/class/leds/charging/delay_on 500
    write /sys/class/leds/charging/delay_off 500

on post-fs-data
    write /sys/class/leds/charging/trigger timer
    write /sys/class/leds/charging/brightness 255
    write /sys/class/leds/charging/delay_on 200
    write /sys/class/leds/charging/delay_off 200

on zygote-start
    write /sys/class/leds/charging/trigger timer
    write /sys/class/leds/charging/brightness 255
    write /sys/class/leds/charging/delay_on 100
    write /sys/class/leds/charging/delay_off 100

on boot
    write /sys/class/leds/charging/trigger none
    write /sys/class/leds/charging/brightness 0
